WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.033
About two billion years ago,

2
00:00:02.033 --> 00:00:03.633
Earth had nuclear reactors.

3
00:00:03.633 --> 00:00:05.367
Nobody built them.

4
00:00:05.667 --> 00:00:07.633
In 1972,

5
00:00:07.633 --> 00:00:09.033
uranium from Gabon

6
00:00:09.033 --> 00:00:11.867
held less uranium-235

7
00:00:11.867 --> 00:00:13.100
than expected.

8
00:00:13.267 --> 00:00:14.567
Fission fingerprints

9
00:00:14.567 --> 00:00:15.467
in the rock

10
00:00:15.467 --> 00:00:16.433
revealed ancient

11
00:00:16.433 --> 00:00:17.967
nuclear reactions.

12
00:00:17.967 --> 00:00:18.867
How could geology

13
00:00:18.867 --> 00:00:20.233
sustain them?

14
00:00:20.533 --> 00:00:21.300
Back then,

15
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:23.300
uranium had a higher share

16
00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:25.533
of that easily split isotope.

17
00:00:25.533 --> 00:00:27.200
Geology concentrated it

18
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:28.867
into rich deposits.

19
00:00:29.033 --> 00:00:30.500
Splitting uranium

20
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:32.033
released neutrons.

21
00:00:32.033 --> 00:00:33.233
Collisions with hydrogen

22
00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:34.233
in groundwater

23
00:00:34.233 --> 00:00:35.033
slowed them,

24
00:00:35.033 --> 00:00:36.133
helping them split

25
00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:37.500
more uranium.

26
00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:39.300
Enough avoided escape

27
00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:40.500
or absorption elsewhere

28
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.533
to keep the chain going.

29
00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:45.167
From one studied
zone's isotopes,

30
00:00:45.167 --> 00:00:46.267
researchers infer

31
00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:47.367
starts and stops:

32
00:00:47.367 --> 00:00:49.067
heating drove water away;

33
00:00:49.067 --> 00:00:51.100
cooling let it return.

34
00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:53.100
Reaction zones in rock.

35
00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:55.567
Heat, not electricity.

36
00:00:55.567 --> 00:00:56.933
Earth had assembled

37
00:00:56.933 --> 00:00:58.667
the conditions for fission,

38
00:00:58.667 --> 00:00:59.500
without machinery.
